From d0f9a144faa56f039b52f1302bdf6b9e804874ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:38:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/32] fix(desktop): web-mode attachment downloads go through
 the browser
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

preview-attachment's download button always called the Electron IPC save
bridge, which does not exist in the web app — every attachment download
failed with 'Desktop file download bridge is unavailable'. Split on the
bridge's presence: Electron keeps the IPC save dialog; web fetches the
authenticated GET /api/files/download URL (same-origin credentials, token
query when the connection carries one) and hands the blob to an <a
download> anchor, failing visibly through the existing error toast on
4xx/5xx.

Filename derivation moved to lib/download-filename.ts (verbatim image
helpers + new attachmentFilename: Content-Disposition name, else basename,
else MIME-derived extension, never an invented one) so media.ts and the
image hook share one seam instead of lib reaching into hooks.
